hadiths[66]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1080","Abu Ayyub narrated that :The Messenger of Allah said: \Four are from the Sunan of the Messengers: Al-Hayat"""""
"1081","Abdullah bin Mas'ud narrated:\We went with Allah's Messenger"
"1082","Sa'eed bin Al-Musayyab narrated from Sa'b bin Abi Waqqas:\The Messenger of Allah refused Uthman bin Ma'zun (when he asked) regarding celibacy"""""
"1083","Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: \When someone whose religion and character you are pleased with proposes to (someone under the care) of one of you"""""
"1084","Abu Hatim Al-Muzani narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: \When someone whose religion and character you are pleased with comes to you then marry (her to) him. If you do not do so"""""
"1085","Jabir narrated that:The Prophet said: \Indeed the woman is married for her religion"""""
"1086","Bakr bin Abdullah Al-Muzani narrated that :Al-Mughirah bin Shu'bah proposed to a woman"
"1087","Abu Al-Balj narrated from Muhammad bin Hatib Al-Jumahi who said that:The Messenger of Allah said: \The distinction between the lawful and the unlawful is the Duff and the voice"""""
"1088","Aishah narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: \Publicize this marriage"""""
"1089","Ar-Rubai bint Muawwidh said:\The morning after the consummation of my marriage"""""
"1090","Abu Hurairah narrated that:When supplicating for the newlywed"
"1091","Ibn Abbas narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: \If anyone of you"""""
"1092","Ibn Abbas narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""If anyone of you, when having sexual intercourse with his wife, says: (Bismillah, Allahumma jannibnash-Shaitana wa jannibish-Shaitana ma razaqtana) 'In the Name of Allah, O Allah! Protect me from Shaitan and protect what you bestow upon us from Shaitan' - then if Allah decrees that they should have a child, Shaitan will not be able to harm him"
"1093","Anas bin Malik narrated:The Messenger of Allah saw some traces of saffron on `Abdur-Rahman bin `Awf so he said: 'What is this?' He said: 'I married a woman for the amount of gold equal to a date stone.' So he said: 'May Allah bless you. Have a banquet"
"1094","Anas bin Malik narrated:\The Prophet had a banquet for Safiyyah bint Huyayy with Sawiq and dates"""""
"1095","(Another chain similar to the narration as no. 1095) :Others have reported this Hadith from Ibn Uyainah"
"1096","Ibn Mas'ud narrated that :The Messenger of Allah said: \Having food on the first day is was is obligatory"""""
"1097","Ibn Umar narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: \Accept the invitation when you are offered"""""
"1098","Abu Mas'ud narrated:\A man named Abu Shu'aib came to a slave of his"""""
"1099","Abu Mas'ud narrated:""A man named Abu Shu'aib came to a slave of his, who was a butcher, and said: 'Prepare some food for me that will be sufficient for five, for I have seen hunger in the face of the Messenger of Allah.' So he prepared some food. Then he sent a message to the Prophet inviting him and those who were sitting with him. When the Prophet stood, he was followed by a man who was not with them when they were invited. When the Messenger of Allah arrive at the door he said to the owner of the house: 'A man who was not with us when you invited us followed us, if you permit him, he will enter.'"" He said: We have permitted him, let him enter"
"1100","Abu Musa narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: \There is no marriage except with a Wali"""""
"1101","Aishah narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: \Whichever woman married without the permission of her Wali her marriage is invalid"""""
"1102","Ibn Abbas narrated that :the Prophet said: \The adulteresses are the ones who marry themselves without Bayyinah (proof)"""""
"1103","Narrated by Ali ibn Hujr, who reported from Sharik ibn Abdullah, from Abu Ishaq — and also narrated by Qutaybah, who reported from Abu Awana, from Abu Ishaq — and also narrated by Muhammad ibn Bashshar, who reported from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq — and also narrated by Abdullah ibn Abi Ziyad, who reported from Zayd ibn Hubab, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: **\There is no marriage without a guardian (wali).\""**\n\nIt is also narrated in this chapter from Aisha"
"1104","Ibn Abi ‘Umar narrated to us; Sufyan ibn ‘Uyaynah narrated to us; from Ibn Jurayj; from Sulayman ibn Musa; from al-Zuhri; from ‘Urwah; from ‘A’ishah, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Any woman who is married without the permission of her guardian, her marriage is void, her marriage is void, her marriage is void. If the marriage is consummated, she is entitled to the mahr (dowry) in return for what he enjoyed of her private part. If they dispute, the ruler is the guardian of the one who has no guardian."" Abu ‘Isa said: This is a Hasan hadith. And Yahya ibn Sa‘id al-Ansari, Yahya ibn Ayyub, Sufyan al-Thawri, and more than one of the preservers (huffaz) narrated from Ibn Jurayj similarly. Abu ‘Isa said: The hadith of Abu Musa is a hadith in which there is disagreement. Isra’il, Sharik ibn ‘Abdullah, Abu ‘Awanah, Zuhayr ibn Mu‘awiyah, and Qays ibn al-Rabi‘ narrated it from Abu Ishaq from Abu Burdah from Abu Musa from the Prophet (ﷺ). Asbat ibn Muhammad and Zayd ibn Hubab narrated from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq from Abu Ishaq from Abu Burdah from Abu Musa from the Prophet (ﷺ). Abu ‘Ubaydah al-Haddad narrated from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq from Abu Burdah from Abu Musa from the Prophet (ﷺ) similarly, but did not mention Abu Ishaq in it. And it has been narrated from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq from Abu Burdah from the Prophet (ﷺ) also. Shu‘bah and al-Thawri narrated from Abu Ishaq from Abu Burdah from the Prophet (ﷺ): ""There is no marriage except with a guardian."" And some companions of Sufyan mentioned from Sufyan from Abu Ishaq from Abu Burdah from Abu Musa, but it is not authentic. The narration of those who narrated from Abu Ishaq from Abu Burdah from Abu Musa from the Prophet (ﷺ): ""There is no marriage except with a guardian,"" is, in my view, more authentic, because their hearing from Abu Ishaq was at different times. Even though Shu‘bah and al-Thawri are more precise and more reliable than all those who narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq, the narration of these (latter) is, in my view, more likely to be correct, because Shu‘bah and al-Thawri heard this hadith from Abu Ishaq in a single sitting. And what indicates that is what Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us; he informed us: Shu‘bah said: I heard Sufyan al-Thawri ask Abu Ishaq: ""Did you hear Abu Burdah say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'There is no marriage except with a guardian'?"" He said: ""Yes."" This hadith indicates that Shu‘bah and al-Thawri heard this hadith at one time. Isra’il is trustworthy and reliable in (narrating from) Abu Ishaq. I heard Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna say: I heard ‘Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi say: I only missed the hadith of al-Thawri from Abu Ishaq that I missed because I relied on Isra’il for it, for he used to bring it more completely. — And the hadith of ‘A’ishah in this chapter from the Prophet (ﷺ): ""There is no marriage except with a guardian"" is, in my view, Hasan. Ibn Jurayj narrated it from Sulayman ibn Musa from al-Zuhri from ‘Urwah from ‘A’ishah from the Prophet (ﷺ). Al-Hajjaj ibn Arta’ah and Ja‘far ibn Rabi‘ah narrated it from al-Zuhri from ‘Urwah from ‘A’ishah from the Prophet (ﷺ). And it was narrated from Hisham ibn ‘Urwah from his father from ‘A’ishah from the Prophet (ﷺ) similarly. Some people of hadith criticized the hadith of al-Zuhri from ‘Urwah from ‘A’ishah from the Prophet (ﷺ). Ibn Jurayj said: Then I met al-Zuhri and asked him, and he denied it. So they weakened this hadith because of this. It was mentioned from Yahya ibn Ma‘in that he said: No one narrated this letter (wording) from Ibn Jurayj except Isma‘il ibn Ibrahim. Yahya ibn Ma‘in said: Isma‘il ibn Ibrahim’s hearing from Ibn Jurayj is not that strong; he only corrected his books from the books of ‘Abd al-Majid ibn ‘Abd al-‘Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad; he did not hear from Ibn Jurayj. And Yahya weakened Isma‘il ibn Ibrahim’s narration from Ibn Jurayj. — The practice in this chapter is upon the hadith of the Prophet (ﷺ): ""There is no marriage except with a guardian,"" among the people of knowledge from the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ), among them ‘Umar ibn al-Khattab, ‘Ali ibn Abi Talib, ‘Abdullah ibn ‘Abbas, Abu Hurayrah, and others. And thus it was narrated from some jurists of the Tabi‘in that they said: ""There is no marriage except with a guardian."" Among them: Sa‘id ibn al-Musayyib, al-Hasan al-Basri, Shurayh, Ibrahim al-Nakha‘i, ‘Umar ibn ‘Abd al-‘Aziz, and others. And this is the saying of Sufyan al-Thawri, al-Awza‘i, ‘Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak, Malik, al-Shafi‘i, Ahmad, and Ishaq."
"1105","Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: \Every Khutbah that does not have the Tashah-hud in it"""""
"1106","Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Prophet said: \A matron should not be given in marriage until she is consulted"""""
"1107","Ibn Abbas narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: \The matron has more right to herself than her Wali"""""
"1108","Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: \An orphan is to be consulted about herself"""""
"1109","Samurah bin Jundab narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: \Whichever woman is given in marriage by two Wali"""""
"1110","Jabir bin Abdullah narrated that:The Prophet said: \Whichever slave gets married without the permission of his owner"""""
"1111","(Another chain) Jabir bin Abdullah narrated that:Abdullah narrated that the Prophet said: \Whichever slave gets married without the permission of his owner"""""
"1112","Abdullah bin Amr bin Rabi'ah narrated from his father:\A woman from Banu Fazarah was married for (the dowry of) two sandals. So the Messenger of Allah said to her: 'Do you approve of (exchanging) yourself and your wealth for two sandals?' She said: 'Yes.'\"" He said: \""So he permitted it"""""
"1113","Sahl bin Sa'd As-Sa'idi narrated that:A woman came to the Messenger of Allah and said: \I present myself to you (for marriage).\"" So she stood for a long time. Then a man said: \""O Messenger of Allah! Marry her to me if you have no need of her.\"" So he said: \""Do you have anything to give her as a dowry?\"" He said: \""I have nothing except this Izar.\"" So the Messenger of Allah said: \""If you give her your Izar then you will have no Izar"""""
"1114","Abu Ayyub narrated that :The Messenger of Allah said: \Four are from the Sunan of the Messengers: Al-Hayat"""""
"1115","Abu Burdah bin Abi Musa narrated from his father that the Messenger of Allah said:\Three will receive their reward twice: A slave who fulfills the rights of Allah and the rights of his owners"""""
"1116","**Narrated by al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Khallal, who narrated to us: Ishaq ibn 'Isa and 'Abdullah ibn Nafi' al-Sa'igh, who both said: Malik ibn Anas informed us, from Abu Hazim ibn Dinar, from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi (may Allah be pleased with him), that:**\n\nA woman came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \I have offered myself to you.\"" She stood for a long while. Then a man said"
"1117","Aishah narrated:\The wife of Rifa'ah Al-Qurzi came to the Messenger of Allah and said: 'I was with Rifa'ah and he divorced me irrevocably. Then I married Abdur-Rahman bin Az-Zubair"""""
"1118","Jabir bin Abdullah and Ali narrated:\The Messenger of Allah cursed the Muhill and the one the Muhallal was done for"""""
"1119","Abdullah bin Mas'ud narrated:\The Messenger of Allah cursed the Muhill and the one the Muhallal was done for"""""
"1120","Abdullah bin Mas'ud narrated:""The Messenger of Allah cursed the Muhill and the one the Muhallal was done for"
"1121","Muhammad bin Ka'b narrated that:Ibn Abbas said: \Mut'ah was only during the beginning of Islam. A man would arrive in a land that he was not familiar with so he would marry a woman for the extent of time that he thought he would remain there. So his Mut'ah was upheld and his case was fine until the (following) Ayah was revealed: Except their wives or what their right hands possess. Then every private part other than those became unlawful"""""
"1122","Muhammad bin Ka'b narrated that:Ibn Abbas said: ""Mut'ah was only during the beginning of Islam. A man would arrive in a land that he was not familiar with so he would marry a woman for the extent of time that he thought he would remain there. So his Mut'ah was upheld and his case was fine until the (following) Ayah was revealed: Except their wives or what their right hands possess. Then every private part other than those became unlawful"
"1123","**Narrated by 'Abdullāh ibn Mas'ūd (may Allāh be pleased with him):**\n\nHe said: \The Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) cursed the one who performs a marriage solely for the purpose of making a woman lawful (*al-muḥill*) and the one for whom she is made lawful (*al-muḥallal lahu*).\""\n\nAbū 'Īsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: \""This is a *ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ* hadith. And Abū Qays al-Awdī's name is 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn Tharwān. This hadith has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) through other chains of narration. The practice (*al-'amal*) according to the people of knowledge among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) — including 'Umar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"
"1124","Ibn Abbas narrated:\The Prophet prohibited marrying a woman along with her paternal aunt or along with her maternal aunt"""""
"1125","Abu Hurairah narrated:\The Messenger of Allah prohibited that a woman be married along with her paternal aunt"""""
"1126","Uqbah bin Amir Al-Juhani narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: \Indeed the conditions most deserving to be fulfilled are those that make the private parts lawful among you"""""
"1127","Ibn Umar narrated:\Ghilan bin Salamah Ath-Thaqafi accepted Islam and he had ten wives in Jahiliyyah who accepted Islam along with him. So the Prophet ordered (him) to chose four (of them)"""""
"1128","Abu Wahb Al-Jaishani narrated that:He heard Ibn Fairuz Ad-Dhailami narrating from his father: \I went to the Prophet and said: 'O Messenger of Allah! I accepted Islam and I had two sisters (as wives).' So the Messenger of Allah said: 'Chose whichever of them you will"""""
"1129","Abu Wahb Al-Jaishani narrated from Ad-Dhahhak bin Fairuz Ad-Dailami from his father:\I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! I accepted Islam and I had two sisters (as wives).' So Messenger of Allah said: 'Chose whichever of them you will"""""
"1130","Ruwaifi bin Thabit narrated that :the Prophet said: \Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day"""""
"1131","Ruwaifi bin Thabit narrated that :the Prophet said: ""Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, then he does not levy his water on someone else's child"
"1132","Abu Mas'ud Al-Ansari narrated:\The Messenger of Allah prohibited the price of a dog"""""
"1133","Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: \A man is not to sell over his brother's sale"""""
"1134","Abu Bakr bin Al-Jahm narrated:\Abu Salamah bin Abdur-Rahman and I visited Fatimah bint Qais. She narrated to us that her husband had divorced her three times"""""
"1135","Abu Bakr bin Al-Jahm narrated:""Abu Salamah bin Abdur-Rahman and I visited Fatimah bint Qais. She narrated to us that her husband had divorced her three times, and he did not leave her with anywhere to live nor any wealth. She said: 'He left ten Aqfizah for me with the son of his uncle: five were of barley, five of wheat.' She said: 'I went to the Messenger of Allah and mentioned that to him.' She said: 'He said: 'He is correct.'"" (She said: ) 'So he ordered me to complete my Iddah in the home of Umm Sharik. But then the Messenger of Allah said to me: ""Umm Sharik's home is visited by Muhajirun, so spend your Iddah in the home of Ibn Umm Maktum, for there you can remove your garments and he will not see you. Then when your Iddah is completed and someone proposed to you come to me."" 'So when my Iddah completed. Abu Jahm and Mu'awiyah proposed to me.' She said: 'I went to the Messenger of Allah and mentioned that to him, and he said: ""As for Mu'awiyah, he is a man with no wealth, and as for Abu Jahm he is a man who is harsh with women."" She said: 'Then Usamah bin Zaid proposed to me, and he married me. So Allah blessed me with Usamah"
"1136","Jabir bin Abdullah narrated:\We practiced Azl while the Qur'an was being revealed"""""
"1137","Abu Sa'eed narrated:\Azl was mentined before the Messenger of Allah and he said: 'Why would one of you do that?"""""
"1138","**Narrated by Mahmūd ibn Ghaylān**, who said: **Abū Dāwūd** narrated to us, who said: **Shuʿbah** informed us, who said: **Abū Bakr ibn Abī al-Jahm** informed me, who said:\n\nI and **Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān** entered upon **Fāṭimah bint Qays**, and she narrated to us that her husband had divorced her with a triple *ṭalāq* (irrevocable divorce) and had not assigned for her any lodging (*suknā*) nor maintenance (*nafaqah*).\n\nShe said: \And he placed with a paternal cousin of his ten *aqfizah* for me — five of barley and five of wheat.\""\n\nShe said: \""So I came to the **Messenger of Allah"
"1139","Aishah narrated that:The Prophet would divide (his time) equally between his wives and said: \O Allah! This is my division in what I have control over"""""
"1140","Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: \When a man has two wives and he is not just between them"""""
"1141","Narrated to us by Ibn Abi 'Umar and Qutaybah, who both said: narrated to us Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Qaz'ah ibn Yahya, from Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him), who said:\n\nThe practice of *'azl* (coitus interruptus) was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he said: **\Why would one of you do that?\""**\n\nIbn Abi 'Umar added in his narration: **\""Let none of you do that.\""**\n\nBoth narrators stated in their version: **\""Indeed"
"1142","Ibn Abbas narrated:\The Prophet returned his daughter Zainab to Abul-As bin Ar-Rabi after six years in the first marriage without renewing the marriage"""""
"1143","Ibn Abbas narrated:""The Prophet returned his daughter Zainab to Abul-As bin Ar-Rabi after six years in the first marriage without renewing the marriage"
"1144","Alqamah narrated that :Ibn Mas'ud was asked about a man who married a woman and he did not stipulate the dowry for her"
"1145","Ali (bin Abi Talib) narrated that The Messenger of Allah said:“Indeed Allah has made unlawful through suckling whatever He made unlawful through lineage.”"
